From: PD rockets contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:50:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] Move a lane by its grip with the pointer, or by its
 step buttons

A lane whose markup holds a [data-kanban-lane-grip] can be dragged by it; lanes without a grip stay put, and card drags are unchanged. While the lane is dragged it carries data-lane-dragging, the lane whose place it would take carries data-lane-drop-target, and a copy of it follows the pointer. A [data-kanban-lane-step] button of -1 or 1 moves the lane one place. Either way the board emits pd-kanban-lane-move with the lane's data-col and the data-col of the lane it now precedes ("" for the end): ids, not positions, so a server can refuse a move whose lanes changed meanwhile. The board moves nothing itself; when the server's answer moves the lanes, they animate from where they were. This ports the column reorder helper of core/board-column-reorder.ts into the board.
